## Edge Function security defaults

Every Edge Function follows this template:

```typescript
// supabase/functions/[name]/index.ts
import { corsHeaders } from "../_shared/cors.ts";
import { z } from "https://esm.sh/zod@3";

const Body = z.object({ /* explicit shape per request */ });

Deno.serve(async (req) => {
  if (req.method === "OPTIONS") return new Response("ok", { headers: corsHeaders });

  // 1. JWT verification (Edge-validated mode only — webhooks/cron use service role)
  const auth = req.headers.get("Authorization");
  if (!auth?.startsWith("Bearer ")) {
    return json({ error: { code: "UNAUTHORIZED", message: "Sign in required" } }, 401);
  }
  const userClient = createClient(SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY, {
    global: { headers: { Authorization: auth } },
  });
  const { data: { user }, error: authErr } = await userClient.auth.getUser();
  if (authErr || !user) {
    return json({ error: { code: "UNAUTHORIZED", message: "Sign in required" } }, 401);
  }

  // 2. Input validation
  let body;
  try { body = Body.parse(await req.json()); }
  catch { return json({ error: { code: "VALIDATION_ERROR", message: "Bad request" } }, 400); }

  // 3. Rate limit (per-user, per-function — see _shared/rate-limit.ts)
  const limited = await rateLimit({ userId: user.id, key: "[name]", windowSec: 60, max: 30 });
  if (limited) return json({ error: { code: "RATE_LIMITED", message: "Slow down" } }, 429);

  // 4. Business logic (use service-role client only after auth + validation pass)
  // ...

  // 5. Response — no stack traces, no internal IDs, no provider tokens
  return json({ /* domain payload only */ }, 200);
});

function json(body: unknown, status: number) {
  return new Response(JSON.stringify(body), {
    status,
    headers: { ...corsHeaders, "Content-Type": "application/json" },
  });
}
```

Per-mode requirements:
- **Edge-validated (client-callable):** all 5 steps above
- **Webhook:** skip step 1 (no JWT); add **signature verification** (step 0) + **idempotency check** (step 2.5) using `payment_idempotency` table
- **Service-role-only (cron):** skip step 1; add **invocation guard** — reject if `req.headers.get("X-Supabase-Source") !== "cron"` (or equivalent for the trigger source)

**CORS:** `_shared/cors.ts` exports two configs — `corsHeaders` (dev: wildcard) and `corsHeadersProd` (prod: explicit allowed origins from `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` env). Functions auto-select based on `Deno.env.get("ENV")`. Never ship wildcard CORS to production.

