## Rate limiting

Every Edge-validated function has a rate limit. Default: **30 req/min per user per function**. Lower for expensive ops (LLM: 10/min; payments: 5/min). Implement via a `rate_limits` table keyed `(user_id, function_name, window_start)` or via Supabase Edge Function KV when available.

```typescript
// supabase/functions/_shared/rate-limit.ts — sketch
export async function rateLimit({ userId, key, windowSec, max }: {
  userId: string; key: string; windowSec: number; max: number;
}) {
  const window = Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000 / windowSec);
  const { data, error } = await serviceRoleClient
    .from("rate_limits")
    .upsert({ user_id: userId, key, window, count: 1 }, {
      onConflict: "user_id,key,window",
      ignoreDuplicates: false,
    })
    .select("count")
    .single();
  if (error) return false; // fail-open on infra errors; Sentry/log this
  return (data?.count ?? 0) > max;
}
```

The `rate_limits` table is part of Foundation backend. RLS denies all client access (server-role only).

