## PII handling

- **Classify on capture.** Northstar §9 (Auth Model) lists profile fields. Tag each as **public**, **internal**, or **sensitive** in the schema migration's contract block. Examples: `email = internal`, `birth_date = sensitive`, `display_name = public`.
- **Sensitive fields never leave the server in cross-user reads.** Use Postgres views or Edge Functions to project to safe columns when serving leaderboards / social feeds.
- **No PII in logs.** Log user IDs (UUIDs), not emails / names / birth dates. Console statements that include `user.email` or similar are a defect.
- **No PII in URLs.** Route params use opaque IDs, never email or full name.
- **Right-to-delete:** every user-data table has a `user_id` foreign key with `ON DELETE CASCADE` to `auth.users`. Sign-out + delete-account flow lives behind a confirm modal; the actual delete runs through an Edge Function (`delete-account`) that double-checks identity before cascading.

