## Audit logging (sensitive operations)

Operations that must be auditable: account deletion, payment events, credit grants/spends, role changes (if RBAC), admin operations.

`audit_log` table (created in Foundation if any audit-worthy op exists in the build):

```sql
CREATE TABLE audit_log (
  id BIGSERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
  user_id UUID REFERENCES auth.users(id),
  actor_id UUID REFERENCES auth.users(id), -- null = system; differs from user_id for admin actions
  action TEXT NOT NULL,
  target_type TEXT,
  target_id TEXT,
  metadata JSONB,
  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now()
);

ALTER TABLE audit_log ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
-- Users see their own audit entries; no inserts/updates/deletes from client
CREATE POLICY "users read own audit" ON audit_log FOR SELECT
  USING (auth.uid() = user_id);
```

Insert via Edge Function only (service-role). Do not expose insert/update/delete to clients. Retention: 12 months default; longer if regulatory.

