## What `/security-audit` adds on top

This file is preventive (every commit). `/security-audit` is the deep audit at pre-deploy:
- Repo-wide secret history scan (`git log --all --diff-filter=D`)
- `npm audit --production`
- Per-table RLS verification against migrations
- OWASP Top 10 checklist
- Build-output scan (`dist/`) for leaked secrets

Both are required: prevention + audit. Skipping either ships insecure software.